WEBVTT

00:01.500 --> 00:03.750
This event for the Sundolls at the end of the year...

00:04.330 --> 00:06.960
Won't you allow JELEE to perform there as well?

00:10.960 --> 00:15.790
And how will the Sunflower Dolls benefit
by letting JELEE perform at the event?

00:16.380 --> 00:18.790
<b>Kimura's
legendary livestream</b>

00:16.380 --> 00:18.790
<b>Certified Banger</b>

00:16.540 --> 00:17.830
Please take a look at this.

00:17.830 --> 00:23.500
I don't want it to end. JUST NO!

00:20.380 --> 00:22.750
This highlight clip alone has 3.1 million views.

00:22.750 --> 00:27.210
The comments section is flooded with requests
for the completed version of this song.

00:28.000 --> 00:32.750
Don't you think featuring the release of this song
would be a huge draw for the event-

00:31.830 --> 00:33.250
I see.

00:33.630 --> 00:36.750
That's a pretty impressive pitch
coming from a high schooler.

00:37.130 --> 00:40.000
There's good momentum and
you have stats to back your claim.

00:40.250 --> 00:40.920
Then do you-

00:40.920 --> 00:41.630
Still.

00:42.080 --> 00:43.830
Is that proposal meaningful?

00:47.170 --> 00:48.710
The people aren't stupid.

00:49.130 --> 00:54.330
If there's nothing more to an idea than generating buzz,
they'll smell the pretense at some point.

00:55.040 --> 00:57.670
The difference between buzz and backlash

00:57.960 --> 01:01.040
ultimately hinges on whether the thought
behind the idea is meaningful.

01:02.170 --> 01:03.580
Do you have an actual answer?

01:04.000 --> 01:06.750
Why are you so eager for this collaboration?

01:07.750 --> 01:10.830
What do you want to accomplish beyond getting numbers?

01:12.040 --> 01:15.080
What I want to do is...!

01:15.500 --> 01:16.170
Kano!

01:17.000 --> 01:17.710
Read this!

01:18.330 --> 01:22.960
<b>Request for JELEE to perform at the Sunflower Dolls'
End-of-Year Live Concert
Hello JELEE,</b>

01:18.340 --> 01:22.960
<b>I apologize for the sudden email.
My name is Yukine Hayakawa, president and
representative director of Hayakawa Productions.</b>

01:18.750 --> 01:22.670
They're asking if we're interested in performing at
the Sunflower Dolls' event at the end of the year.

01:23.080 --> 01:23.710
Huh?

01:24.500 --> 01:27.170
Sounds like... Mahiru asked for this.

01:29.000 --> 01:30.130
What do you think?

01:30.710 --> 01:32.380
We can say no.

01:32.670 --> 01:33.540
Nono-tan...

01:35.000 --> 01:35.920
I...

01:36.880 --> 01:39.500
What I want to do...

01:42.170 --> 01:43.130
Ms. Yukine.

01:43.130 --> 01:43.920
Hmm?

01:44.500 --> 01:47.130
This is something I realized quite recently,

01:47.790 --> 01:52.250
but when someone does something for me,
I want to reciprocate.

01:52.630 --> 01:56.750
This offer. I want to take it.

01:58.040 --> 02:01.130
<b>Final Episode:</b>

01:59.670 --> 02:03.080
So yeah, tonight's the night you've been waiting for.

02:03.080 --> 02:06.880
The virtual gig at Shibuya's Miyashita Park,
in collaboration with the Sundolls!

02:07.460 --> 02:10.080
Are you all ready to take part?

02:10.080 --> 02:13.540
<b>Castella    Of course!</b>

02:10.420 --> 02:10.670
<b>Hachidai     Can't Wait</b>

02:10.670 --> 02:13.540
<b>SoySauce    Makes up for the Halloween gig</b>

02:11.000 --> 02:13.540
<b>got an umbrella ready</b>

02:11.250 --> 02:13.540
<b>Hikarin     Make it the best gig ever</b>

02:11.540 --> 02:13.540
<b>Yacchi    a blue plastic umbrella</b>

02:11.880 --> 02:13.540
<b>already in Shibuya</b>

02:11.880 --> 02:13.040
Good to see!

02:14.920 --> 02:17.330
W-we're not forgetting anything, are we?

02:17.580 --> 02:19.080
No! We're all set!

02:19.380 --> 02:21.500
Uhh, what's this?

02:21.500 --> 02:24.000
<b>Sunflower
Dolls</b>

02:21.710 --> 02:23.710
Wow! The real Little JELEE!

02:22.130 --> 02:23.710
Provocative marketing?

02:24.540 --> 02:29.710
"Hayakawa's tactic to turn the
doxing into buzz is ingenious."

02:25.460 --> 02:28.210
Let's make the fans' hearts melt together today!

02:26.790 --> 02:30.290
<b>Provocative marketing or elaborate publicity stunt?!
The story behind Yukine Hayakawa's latest live gig.</b>

02:30.290 --> 02:31.960
Oh, that rumor?

02:32.130 --> 02:37.790
Here to blast all those comments away
is invincible VTuber Nox Ryugasaki...

02:38.000 --> 02:39.210
I mean, JELEE!

02:39.210 --> 02:41.290
Right then, goodbye world!

02:44.750 --> 02:46.960
It's the actual day.

02:47.710 --> 02:49.960
Will you... be all right?

02:52.460 --> 02:53.420
Nono-tan?

02:53.710 --> 02:54.420
Huh?

02:55.000 --> 02:56.670
Are you worried about Miss Mahiru?

02:56.830 --> 03:00.960
Or... whether you'll be able to sing?

03:02.380 --> 03:04.830
I'm not really sure which.

03:05.330 --> 03:06.960
Or about your mother?

03:08.420 --> 03:09.290
I dunno.

03:10.710 --> 03:13.920
What I want to do... What I'm scared of...

03:15.080 --> 03:16.000
All I know is...

03:18.210 --> 03:19.420
I want to sing.

03:19.830 --> 03:22.420
That at least is definitely true.

03:23.880 --> 03:24.710
Okay, over here!

03:27.500 --> 03:28.960
So tonight's the night.

03:29.710 --> 03:30.580
It is.

03:31.080 --> 03:35.960
There's so much hype. My friends, the fans...
Everyone says they've been waiting for this day.

03:36.540 --> 03:37.790
Of course they have.

03:45.920 --> 03:47.790
Whoa, there's a huge crowd already!

03:56.290 --> 03:57.330
Nono-tan...

03:57.710 --> 03:58.880
You okay?

04:01.750 --> 04:03.380
Sorry. I'm fine.

04:03.380 --> 04:04.130
Let's go.

04:13.210 --> 04:16.540
love, love, weather

04:17.460 --> 04:18.670
lovely weather

04:18.670 --> 04:22.080
Everything surely is lovely weather

04:23.460 --> 04:25.880
A camera for live streaming and three 3D models.

04:24.670 --> 04:27.630
Manipulating even the sun (just might be unbeatable)

04:25.880 --> 04:27.670
They've really poured funds into this.

04:27.630 --> 04:29.250
The world is the backdrop

04:27.960 --> 04:30.130
Money's rather amazing, isn't it?

04:29.830 --> 04:32.540
Because when rain would be more lovely

04:32.000 --> 04:34.330
<b>MERO</b>

04:32.290 --> 04:33.670
Lovely!

04:32.540 --> 04:36.330
Make it rain as well, go ahead and get soaked

04:44.790 --> 04:45.500
...folder

04:45.500 --> 04:48.540
A dream, want to dream, it's not a dream

04:48.540 --> 04:51.460
Dance, drops, drops of sound

04:51.460 --> 04:54.170
Like tears, tears aren't so bad...

04:54.630 --> 04:56.920
All right, thank you very much!

04:57.670 --> 05:01.580
That was the Sunflower Dolls singing "Lovely Weather"!

04:58.130 --> 04:59.330
Thanks everyone!

05:02.210 --> 05:04.250
Okay, here I go!

05:02.790 --> 05:05.290
So cute! You're so cute!

05:04.880 --> 05:05.500
Yup.

05:05.290 --> 05:06.630
Whew, we're done!

05:14.920 --> 05:17.960
Your MC for the rest of the show is still me,
Yukochi, with 1.2 million followers.

05:17.960 --> 05:19.580
Oh, news flash time.

05:23.420 --> 05:24.460
Nono-tan…

05:24.790 --> 05:27.380
The number just jumped up to 1.2 million and 5 thousand followers.

05:24.920 --> 05:27.080
Are you still scared?

05:28.460 --> 05:30.040
Aww, thank you, thank you!

05:31.080 --> 05:32.170
Pathetic, right?

05:32.960 --> 05:36.460
I've never gone on stage before without a reason to sing.

05:37.000 --> 05:38.130
Besides...

05:40.670 --> 05:45.630
People who hated on me back then and fans I let down

05:45.630 --> 05:46.500
Nono-tan!

05:46.210 --> 05:48.420
are probably in that crowd.

05:46.790 --> 05:48.000
Nonoka!

06:00.880 --> 06:01.830
Thanks.

06:02.330 --> 06:03.290
After all...

06:04.420 --> 06:06.000
I'm JELEE now, aren't I?

06:07.000 --> 06:12.040
Going on, let's welcome JELEE,
currently trending big on PikPok.

06:12.420 --> 06:15.540
I hear today they'll be presenting
live singing via virtual gig.

06:15.540 --> 06:20.540
The song is the finished version from the touching
disbandment announcement stream that swept the nation.

06:19.000 --> 06:20.540
Don't you ever come back.

06:20.710 --> 06:21.460
She's so done.

06:21.750 --> 06:23.170
Was she ever that popular?

06:23.170 --> 06:24.250
Ugh, no thanks.

06:24.250 --> 06:25.290
I had faith in you.

06:24.580 --> 06:26.380
Her life as a singer is over.

06:25.500 --> 06:26.750
No one wants you!

06:26.750 --> 06:27.830
You've got some nerve!

06:27.420 --> 06:28.710
Uhhhh, yikes.

06:28.420 --> 06:29.420
Super lame.

06:29.420 --> 06:31.040
She doesn't deserve to be an idol.

06:30.290 --> 06:31.330
I really hate her.

06:31.040 --> 06:31.830
Get lost!

06:42.830 --> 06:46.000
All right JELEE, can you say
a few words about your song?

06:48.880 --> 06:50.920
Uh? Hello?

06:51.330 --> 06:51.880
Kano!

06:51.880 --> 06:52.670
Nono-tan?!

06:52.670 --> 06:59.330
Umm... JELEE? I'm sure so much went
into completing this song.

06:53.380 --> 06:54.250
What's wrong?!

06:54.250 --> 06:55.420
The live stream's already on!

06:55.420 --> 06:57.290
What's going on?! Should we go check?

06:59.670 --> 07:03.170
I guess your heart must be so full right now?

07:03.710 --> 07:05.880
As for me, my tummy's definitely not full right now.

07:05.880 --> 07:06.670
I...

07:07.830 --> 07:09.250
Oops, there's the song.

07:09.250 --> 07:10.080
Go ahead.

07:17.250 --> 07:20.580
To that sea... where the snow falls...

07:19.080 --> 07:20.630
Uh? Is she singing?

07:20.040 --> 07:20.790
Is she okay?

07:20.790 --> 07:21.920
Is her mic off?

07:22.500 --> 07:23.960
She isn't singing loud enough.

07:22.790 --> 07:23.670
JELEE...

07:24.290 --> 07:25.330
You okay?

07:26.540 --> 07:27.920
Yo, what's the matter?

07:28.540 --> 07:29.420
Hello?

07:30.290 --> 07:31.460
We can't hear you!

07:39.380 --> 07:40.580
Nonoka!

07:47.880 --> 07:50.330
Take a good look in front of you, idiot!

07:57.380 --> 07:59.290
Hey, Kano. Make one.

07:59.920 --> 08:03.040
A big aquarium, right in Shibuya!

08:07.080 --> 08:09.130
Kano!

08:15.790 --> 08:22.500
A cluttered room and a shiny mic

08:23.250 --> 08:28.880
The wrong spelling of a name in alphabet letters

08:30.630 --> 08:37.670
Chatting about nothing before goodnight

08:33.170 --> 08:33.960
Yes!

08:38.170 --> 08:43.710
A favorite chocolate I always buy in bulk

08:44.000 --> 08:51.250
"The moon is beautiful tonight," a message I received from you

08:44.080 --> 08:47.380
That moving Little JELEE model. Did you do that, too?

08:47.710 --> 08:50.830
'Course not. I paid a huge express fee to commission it.

08:51.170 --> 08:54.130
I used up all of the ad revenue we had built up.

08:51.250 --> 09:00.960
A light, full and round, was floating in the night sky

08:52.420 --> 08:54.420
<b>Channel analytics</b>

08:52.420 --> 08:54.420
<b>Your estimated revenue:</b>

08:54.830 --> 08:56.920
Money can be rather amazing.

08:57.710 --> 08:59.830
All right, here comes the best part!

09:05.630 --> 09:20.500
On this night, this dark night,
I went and found a light that will never fade

09:10.460 --> 09:11.460
This...

09:20.750 --> 09:34.420
That's why I can keep on swimming,
even if I can't hear the sound of snow anymore

09:35.330 --> 09:50.580
The jellyfish's song (my song) rings out
so it will reach you come tomorrow

09:59.380 --> 10:04.380
<b>Shibuya became one big aquarium!!</b>

10:04.710 --> 10:08.710
Thank you very much. JELEE, everyone!

10:08.880 --> 10:11.630
Wow, that was just the best!

10:12.630 --> 10:13.670
Kano!

10:16.420 --> 10:17.290
Mahiru!

10:23.790 --> 10:24.580
Ahh!

10:26.080 --> 10:26.960
Mahiru!

10:26.080 --> 10:26.960
Kano!

10:33.250 --> 10:35.290
What are those two doing?

10:37.250 --> 10:41.130
Kanoooo!

10:42.130 --> 10:43.000
Whoa!

10:47.460 --> 10:50.040
Wow! Did the fans get the umbrellas ready?

10:50.040 --> 10:53.000
Yeah! These two helped make it happen!

10:53.500 --> 10:56.210
A virtual aquarium made up of blue umbrellas.

10:56.210 --> 10:57.580
Kano's idea, clearly.

10:58.080 --> 10:59.880
I didn't actually do anything!

11:01.130 --> 11:02.000
Okay...

11:02.790 --> 11:03.790
Mahiru!

11:03.790 --> 11:08.500
I'm sorry! I said some really
thoughtless things and hurt you.

11:08.500 --> 11:10.750
Not at all. I'm the one who's sorry.

11:11.080 --> 11:13.710
I only thought about myself and just up and left.

11:14.080 --> 11:15.000
But hey!

11:15.540 --> 11:17.750
I kept my promise, you know!

11:30.250 --> 11:31.290
It's over.

11:32.460 --> 11:35.210
Yeah, all over.

11:36.380 --> 11:38.710
How was it? Working with my mom?

11:39.380 --> 11:40.290
Well...

11:40.830 --> 11:42.380
Professionals are ruthless!

11:40.960 --> 11:47.170
<b>To Our Guests
Thank you for coming out to the Sunflower Dolls and
JELEE's collaboration concert tonight.</b>

11:43.330 --> 11:46.710
Or rather... Ms. Yukine's a little extreme, isn't she?

11:47.170 --> 11:55.000
<b>We are truly fortunate that you chose to spend your precious last day
of the year at our show. The entire staff is sincerely grateful.
There was more to this collaboration than meets the eye.
Of course it was a collaboration between the Sunflower Dolls and JELEE,
as well as one between real and virtual entertainment.</b>

11:49.130 --> 11:49.880
You noticed?

11:50.500 --> 11:55.380
That's someone whose career is like, her whole life.

11:55.000 --> 11:59.670
<b>But for those who have deeper knowledge of the Sunflower Dolls,
this was also arguably a collaboration between the past and present.
If the event today served to convey the emotional significance of that opportunity
in regards to the history behind it, we couldn't be happier.</b>

11:56.080 --> 11:57.130
Yeah.

11:57.790 --> 11:58.670
For better...

12:00.250 --> 12:01.250
or for worse.

12:05.000 --> 12:07.170
Still, I'm glad I did this.

12:09.880 --> 12:10.790
Yeah?

12:11.580 --> 12:14.670
<b>The Sunflower Dolls will continue to move forward with their faces toward the
sun, three flowers blooming proud and tall to guide lost people everywhere.</b>

12:11.590 --> 12:14.670
<b>We hope that you will keep supporting Mero Setou, Momoko Yanagi,
and Akari Suzumura.
Yukine Hayakwa</b>

12:12.580 --> 12:13.710
What about you, Kano?

12:14.920 --> 12:15.920
Well...

12:16.750 --> 12:18.750
I was empty all this time.

12:19.330 --> 12:25.130
<b>Sunflower Dolls</b>

12:19.330 --> 12:25.130
<b>Mero Setou</b>

12:19.340 --> 12:25.130
<b>Momoko Yanagi
Akari Suzumura</b>

12:19.580 --> 12:24.750
Even when I was told I was shining,
there was nothing inside of me.

12:25.670 --> 12:26.420
Yeah?

12:27.040 --> 12:29.960
Remember what you told me?

12:30.670 --> 12:32.500
To sing for your sake?

12:33.330 --> 12:34.750
That made me so happy.

12:35.540 --> 12:39.670
But that's why, when I thought
I lost both you and my mom,

12:40.500 --> 12:43.250
I just didn't know anymore.

12:47.080 --> 12:48.880
But hey. Look!

12:50.040 --> 12:51.710
I realized something today.

12:52.170 --> 12:54.420
Something that's probably never gonna change.

12:54.420 --> 12:55.000
Yeah!

12:55.000 --> 12:57.380
The reason Kano Yamanouchi sings!

12:57.130 --> 13:00.630
<b>Japan Trends
#PleaseKeepSupportingUsIn2025
New Year's Prizes for 10,000 lucky winners!
Promotion by Doga Kobo
#HappyNewYear!
#SunflowerDolls&JELEE
#JELEE
#AquariumInShibuya
#SunflowerDolls</b>

12:57.880 --> 13:01.080
See, I want to be a reason for
people to keep looking forward.

13:01.670 --> 13:03.710
For the fans who support me...

13:04.290 --> 13:06.500
No, not just them.

13:07.290 --> 13:13.250
Anyone lost about what they really love, and
anyone who struggles every day and hates the world.

13:14.170 --> 13:18.630
And even the ones who used
to make fun of me, just everyone!

13:18.630 --> 13:21.920
I want them to feel happy,
that life's fun, and just the best!

13:22.330 --> 13:29.080
That life's worth living until the next gig,
that they want to pursue JELEE's dreams along with us!

13:29.630 --> 13:33.170
I want to make everyone's days sparkle and shine.

13:33.580 --> 13:35.790
That's why I want to sing!

13:38.130 --> 13:39.920
You know, Kano.

13:40.540 --> 13:41.290
Huh?

13:41.750 --> 13:43.830
That's how you show fans love.

13:47.000 --> 13:47.880
I guess!

13:52.290 --> 13:54.580
Yo, they say it's time to head out soon.

13:54.580 --> 13:55.290
Really?

13:55.670 --> 13:56.750
Then we should get going-

13:55.960 --> 13:57.170
Oh look, everyone!

13:59.000 --> 14:01.500
Huh! That's a nice touch.

14:01.750 --> 14:02.960
There's my name.

14:02.540 --> 14:04.210
<b>Nox Ryugasaki</b>

14:03.210 --> 14:05.580
There's something really nice about this, huh?

14:05.920 --> 14:07.880
Yeah, I guess.

14:07.790 --> 14:10.000
<b>Kimura</b>

14:08.170 --> 14:10.080
Oh! It says "Kimura"!

14:10.080 --> 14:11.250
I'm flattered.

14:11.830 --> 14:13.420
Why do you have two names, Mahiru?

14:12.960 --> 14:14.960
<b>Yoru Umitsuki / Mahiru Kouzuki</b>

14:13.880 --> 14:15.670
Besides, did you want your real name up there?

14:15.670 --> 14:18.670
It's fine! It's who I am.

14:19.460 --> 14:21.580
I see. That's very you, Mahiru.

14:21.920 --> 14:23.040
Very cool.

14:24.580 --> 14:28.080
You know, I discovered
a new side of you today, Yukine-pi.

14:28.790 --> 14:29.830
What do you mean?

14:29.830 --> 14:31.960
You're more kindhearted than you seem.

14:33.460 --> 14:37.380
I mean, that credit roll.
You recognize her for who she is, don't you?

14:38.330 --> 14:39.630
Don't be silly.

14:40.460 --> 14:43.500
She graduated and moved on
from being Nonoka Tachibana.

14:44.330 --> 14:51.380
Knowing that, it only makes sense for the producer
to use her real name, don't you think?

14:46.920 --> 14:50.710
<b>Kano Hayakawa</b>

15:22.670 --> 15:24.040
Hey, look at this.

15:24.540 --> 15:25.130
Hmm?

15:25.460 --> 15:29.250
The stream from today.
There were 50,000 live viewers at its peak.

15:29.670 --> 15:30.830
Gimme that a sec!

15:30.830 --> 15:32.830
<b>The Sunflower Dolls & JELEE's New Year's Eve
Stream Reaches More Than 50,000 live viewers!!</b>

15:30.840 --> 15:32.830
<b>The miraculous moment it went passed 50,000 viewers</b>

15:34.750 --> 15:36.960
50,000 people. 50,000 people?!

15:36.960 --> 15:38.080
Yes!

15:38.580 --> 15:41.540
Um... Congratulations?

15:42.830 --> 15:45.250
Maybe we can leave the stats for later.

15:45.250 --> 15:47.040
What do you mean?

15:47.250 --> 15:49.250
<b>The Sunflower Dolls & JELEE's New Year's Eve
Stream Reaches More Than 50,000 live viewers!</b>

15:47.250 --> 15:49.250
<b>The miraculous moment it went passed 50,000 viewers</b>

15:47.500 --> 15:49.130
Wait, don't you know?

15:50.170 --> 15:53.580
A fully packed Tokyo Dome
is an audience of 50,000 people.

15:54.290 --> 15:56.170
Uh? Why does that matter?

15:57.130 --> 15:59.710
Well, if anything, I guess...

16:00.830 --> 16:02.830
I managed to do something for my mom.

16:06.880 --> 16:09.380
<b>University
Entry
Exam
Venue</b>

16:14.420 --> 16:17.420
You cut out again. Koharu?

16:17.420 --> 16:18.710
That's weird.

16:20.710 --> 16:24.750
Well... I guess we can meet up offline, if you want.

16:24.750 --> 16:26.540
Oh. Nah, not today.

16:26.540 --> 16:27.250
Huh?!

16:27.500 --> 16:29.540
Hey, that's not what I mean.

16:29.540 --> 16:32.130
I'm actually in downtime right now.

16:32.460 --> 16:34.330
You did more stuff?

16:35.130 --> 16:37.790
Guess that's cool. Like a new VTuber fit.

16:40.290 --> 16:43.630
The time has come for me
to announce that I, Shizue Baba...

16:44.250 --> 16:47.630
...turned forty-two today!

16:48.250 --> 16:49.750
Mom, you're so cute!

16:49.750 --> 16:51.330
My dear sister Mahiru!

16:51.420 --> 16:55.000
There's something I desperately need your advice on!

16:55.460 --> 16:56.710
Wh-what's this?

16:56.710 --> 17:00.080
If I want to sing a cover to upload,
what kind of mic should I use?

17:00.080 --> 17:01.670
So I can go viral?!

17:02.460 --> 17:05.330
Uh, shouldn't you focus on your studies first?

17:07.080 --> 17:11.290
Ah well, something around 10,000 yen is fine for a start.

17:11.830 --> 17:13.920
What? Who does that?

17:13.920 --> 17:16.330
Well, this is Yukine-pi we're talking about.

17:22.330 --> 17:24.830
<b>Congratulations!</b>

17:22.330 --> 17:24.830
<b>Graduation</b>

17:22.340 --> 17:24.830
<b>Ceremony</b>

17:25.040 --> 17:26.330
Here, Mahiru!

17:27.080 --> 17:27.830
Huh?

17:33.130 --> 17:38.330
<b>Happy Graduation!</b>

17:36.880 --> 17:38.330
Are you kidding me?!

17:38.580 --> 17:42.920
Today's graduation day, and this many of
you are at home watching this live stream?

17:42.920 --> 17:51.500
<b>Uses doxing as fodder for a joke</b>

17:43.210 --> 17:51.500
<b>Year of the Bull    student council president (23)</b>

17:43.460 --> 17:51.500
<b>This your 5th year, Nox?</b>

17:43.790 --> 17:51.500
<b>Yotsuhashi    You know you're one of us</b>

17:44.960 --> 17:47.880
Knowing you're outcasts who couldn't
even go to your own graduations,

17:47.880 --> 17:50.960
lemme at least give you some words
to send you off into the world.

17:53.830 --> 18:00.080
There'll be plenty of people in life who say
you're not normal or that you're weird.

18:00.330 --> 18:01.500
But if no one else,

18:01.790 --> 18:07.080
Nox Ryugasaki here will always be on your side!

18:07.670 --> 18:10.330
Um, you're Kimura, aren't you?

18:10.790 --> 18:11.500
Huh?

18:11.790 --> 18:15.880
Congratulations on your graduation!
M-may I ask for your autograph?

18:17.830 --> 18:19.130
My autograph?!

18:19.500 --> 18:24.710
I don't have any friends, and no other passions...

18:24.920 --> 18:28.250
But JELEE's song always helped me. So...!

18:29.500 --> 18:32.380
Then I guess we're pretty similar.

18:32.380 --> 18:33.130
Huh?

18:33.420 --> 18:34.500
You'll be fine!  

18:34.500 --> 18:37.960
Even if you don't have any friends or anything you love,

18:38.420 --> 18:43.170
I promise JELEE's songs won't ever let you feel alone.

18:38.880 --> 18:43.960
<b>Someday when you're famous,
let's play a piano duet together!
Kimura</b>

18:43.960 --> 18:48.330
<b>Graduation</b>

18:58.500 --> 19:01.130
I made your dream come true, Mom!

19:03.500 --> 19:04.330
Ah.

19:09.670 --> 19:11.130
Look how you've grown.

19:12.540 --> 19:15.380
Congratulations on your graduation, Kano.

19:33.250 --> 19:34.040
Yo!

19:35.380 --> 19:37.210
So you went to your graduation.

19:37.210 --> 19:39.040
I did. What about you?

19:39.210 --> 19:40.540
Live streamed from my room.

19:40.540 --> 19:41.710
Sticking to your guns, huh?

19:42.580 --> 19:43.960
Nono-tan in a school uniform-

19:43.960 --> 19:46.460
Both of you, congratulations on your graduation.

19:46.460 --> 19:47.540
You too, Mei.

19:47.540 --> 19:48.210
Congrats.

19:48.210 --> 19:49.630
Sorry I'm late!

19:49.630 --> 19:51.460
Hey everyone, congrats on graduating!

19:51.460 --> 19:51.920
Congrats!

19:51.460 --> 19:52.960
Congratulations.

19:53.250 --> 19:54.920
Haven't use these paints in ages!

19:54.920 --> 19:56.880
Okay, let's do this!

19:59.670 --> 20:02.460
They request we do what we want with this!

20:02.460 --> 20:04.210
All right!

20:06.790 --> 20:09.000
Painting this is gonna take forever, huh?

20:09.960 --> 20:10.790
Take that!

20:11.580 --> 20:12.500
Me too!

20:12.500 --> 20:14.420
Oh no you don't!

20:14.960 --> 20:16.920
Don't let me fall, y'hear?!

20:16.920 --> 20:18.540
Uh, we have a stepladder!

20:18.540 --> 20:20.080
Hee hee hee hee...

20:20.080 --> 20:20.920
Hee!

20:20.920 --> 20:22.330
D-don't do that!

20:25.790 --> 20:27.540
Hey, stop slacking off!

20:28.460 --> 20:31.790
Here's popular illustrator Yoru Umitsuki, hard at work.

20:32.170 --> 20:33.130
Yay!

20:35.170 --> 20:37.380
Umm, what are you doing?

20:38.500 --> 20:39.420
Here, open wide!

20:39.920 --> 20:41.750
Those are my snacks!

20:42.000 --> 20:45.000
<b>A gift from the Watase Atelier of Painting
Original idea by</b>

20:42.000 --> 20:45.000
<b>Yoru Umitsuki</b>

20:45.250 --> 20:48.540
You know, I wish we could hang out like this forever.

20:48.790 --> 20:49.750
Yeah.

20:50.330 --> 20:52.790
But we can't really, can we?

20:55.380 --> 20:56.670
Hey, did you know?

20:56.670 --> 21:01.210
A human's internal clock actually runs on a 25 hour day.

21:01.210 --> 21:02.580
Is that so?

21:03.460 --> 21:10.290
I've been thinking lately, then shouldn't
a day just be 25 hours to fit us?

21:19.420 --> 21:22.920
You know, there's so much more I still wanna do.

21:23.170 --> 21:27.290
I want to create a whole lot more songs
and put on more gigs.

21:27.750 --> 21:32.290
I want to go on a trip with you all and spend
the entire night laughing over stupid stuff that sucks.

21:33.460 --> 21:34.960
There just isn't enough time.

21:35.460 --> 21:37.500
No way there's enough.

21:38.460 --> 21:39.750
Don't you think so?

21:40.580 --> 21:43.080
Yeah. Definitely not enough.

21:46.580 --> 21:47.920
But you know, Kano.

21:48.420 --> 21:51.580
I know what to do to solve that problem.

21:51.580 --> 21:52.330
Huh?

21:53.330 --> 21:57.130
Tomorrow, the day after, and beyond that,
we just have to always be together.

21:57.130 --> 21:58.130
Easy, right?

22:02.130 --> 22:03.210
Mahiru!

22:03.210 --> 22:04.290
Huh? Whoa!

22:04.830 --> 22:05.670
Ow!

22:05.670 --> 22:07.420
Why would you do that?

22:11.420 --> 22:13.830
I like hanging out with everyone in town.

22:18.420 --> 22:25.210
When I'm with the three others, drifting around
the bustling city as aimlessly as a jellyfish,

22:24.080 --> 22:27.790
The second hand won't stop, there's no time to be feeling down

22:25.880 --> 22:29.210
I have fun no matter the situation.

22:27.790 --> 22:36.380
Every day is packed, a list full of things I want to do

22:30.750 --> 22:32.960
We don't need colorful neon lights.

22:33.830 --> 22:36.210
We know we have what it takes

22:36.580 --> 22:43.330
Talking takes too long so I'll make it brief with a song

22:37.630 --> 22:39.040
to choose our own colors.

22:43.080 --> 22:44.750
I'm so hungry!

22:43.540 --> 22:51.210
Ever since that night I found you, the rhythm started accelerating

22:45.080 --> 22:47.130
Hey, why don't we go somewhere to eat?

22:47.540 --> 22:48.330
Great idea.

22:48.330 --> 22:49.420
Let's do it!

22:49.880 --> 22:50.630
Off we go!

22:51.210 --> 22:52.420
Do we have to run?

22:52.630 --> 22:53.580
We should!

22:53.580 --> 23:01.420
Only having 24 hours in a day isn't nearly enough

22:53.580 --> 22:54.670
Let's go!

22:55.420 --> 22:56.830
What should we eat?!

22:56.830 --> 22:59.330
Yoru Umitsuki's jellyfish can't swim.

23:00.080 --> 23:03.330
I mean, the man at the aquarium said as much.

23:01.750 --> 23:08.420
I haven't caught up to the night yet and morning's already coming

23:03.960 --> 23:09.080
That's why I want to draw to show
how those jellyfish can shine!

23:06.880 --> 23:09.380
<b>A gift from the Watase Atelier of Painting
Original idea by</b>

23:08.540 --> 23:20.830
Just one hour more would do, I want to gaze
on that moon, the same moon as yours

23:12.580 --> 23:18.000
Because you see, to me those jellyfish...

23:18.960 --> 23:20.670
Maybe they usually go with the flow,

23:20.920 --> 23:24.790
but once they put their minds to it,
they can shine on their own.

23:21.040 --> 23:27.670
When I fell in love with the present that's ordinary
the future got a bit more vibrant

23:25.920 --> 23:28.380
That's what makes those cute jellyfish

23:27.670 --> 23:33.210
That's how I waited for tomorrow

23:30.080 --> 23:33.630
what I love, from the very bottom of my heart!
